# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Cross-origin isolation (L6): the browser only exposes SharedArrayBuffer to an
# isolated page, and that is what lets the Python Worker block on input() with
# Atomics.wait. The same two headers are the entry ticket for any wasm-hosted
# compiler with threads (see reports/Rust and Go execution on iPad).
#
# require-corp would break cross-origin subresources — Altitude has none, by
# the zero-CDN rule, so nothing here is a trade-off in practice.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
